; horner-bank-fp64.cfta - a degree-23 polynomial whose coefficients
; are the run's data. The library's BANK_EXT worked example.
;
; docs/SEQUENCER.md revision 2, R3: with `flags.BANK_EXT` the image
; carries NO constant section. `n_consts` still says how many
; constants the program addresses - twenty-four here - and every run
; supplies exactly that many format-width values in a bank buffer:
;
;     positive-run horner-bank-fp64.cftp --a x.bin \
;                  --bank horner-bank-fp64.exp.bank
;
; One image, many polynomials. That is the point of the feature and
; the reason docs/ATLAS.md asked for it: one image per positive with
; the levers, the clock and the pass riding as data, loaded once
; instead of rebuilt per run.
;
; The image is therefore exactly 32 + 8 * n_insns bytes, and its
; SHA-256 is a hash of the SCHEDULE alone - which is why
; `cft_program_digest` hashes the image and the bank together. Two
; runs of this file with two banks are two different computations and
; they have two different digests, while the image's own hash is the
; same in both. Both numbers matter and they are not the same number.
;
;   r0    x, the evaluation point (stream a)
;   r3    the accumulator
;   deposits: p(x)
;
; Twenty-four coefficients is past the sixteen a four-bit operand
; field reaches, so the FMAs from C16 on are emitted in the indexed
; (`kx`) form automatically - the bank index rides in the immediate.
; Nothing about the arithmetic changes, which is exactly the property
; docs/ENCLOSE.md had to demonstrate when the feature landed.
;
; COPYSIGN is how the accumulator is loaded: magnitude of a, sign of
; b, both the same constant, so it is C0 exactly - for -0 and for a
; NaN too - and it signals nothing. An ADD of +0 would flatten -0 to
; +0 and a MUL by one would round a subnormal's product; this does
; neither, and it is the reason the opcode is worth having.

.format   fp64
.deposits 1
.bank     external

.const    C0
.const    C1
.const    C2
.const    C3
.const    C4
.const    C5
.const    C6
.const    C7
.const    C8
.const    C9
.const    C10
.const    C11
.const    C12
.const    C13
.const    C14
.const    C15
.const    C16
.const    C17
.const    C18
.const    C19
.const    C20
.const    C21
.const    C22
.const    C23

.reg      x   = r0
.reg      acc = r3

copysign acc, C0, C0
fma acc, acc, x, C1
fma acc, acc, x, C2
fma acc, acc, x, C3
fma acc, acc, x, C4
fma acc, acc, x, C5
fma acc, acc, x, C6
fma acc, acc, x, C7
fma acc, acc, x, C8
fma acc, acc, x, C9
fma acc, acc, x, C10
fma acc, acc, x, C11
fma acc, acc, x, C12
fma acc, acc, x, C13
fma acc, acc, x, C14
fma acc, acc, x, C15
fma acc, acc, x, C16
fma acc, acc, x, C17
fma acc, acc, x, C18
fma acc, acc, x, C19
fma acc, acc, x, C20
fma acc, acc, x, C21
fma acc, acc, x, C22
fma acc, acc, x, C23
deposit acc
halt
